VISHWANEED
Multi-Vendor Marketplace – Important
Requirements
Prepared as a practical reference for marketplace development
1. Business Model & Marketplace Structure
• Vishwaneed is a technology-enabled multi-vendor marketplace connecting rural producers/vendors directly with
customers.
• Initial focus: Food Products, including millets, millet-based products and jaggery.
• Future categories: Handicrafts, Clothing, Home & Lifestyle and other Made-in-India products.
• Primary revenue model: commission on successful marketplace sales from vendors.
2. Three Core Panels
Panel
Main Purpose
Customer Panel
Vendor Panel
Browse products, search/filter, cart, checkout, payment, tracking, reviews and complaints.
Registration, KYC/documents, products, inventory, orders, sales, commission, settlements and complaints.
Admin Panel
Vendor verification, product approval, quality control, orders, payments, commission, settlements, refunds, complaints, reviews and reports.
3. Customer-Side Requirements
• Registration & Login: mobile/email registration, OTP verification, login/logout, forgot password.
• Profile & Address: customer profile, address management and multiple delivery addresses.
• Home Page: featured products, trending products, new arrivals, best sellers, categories, vendor highlights, regional
products and offers.
• Catalogue & Search: categories, search, filters and sorting.
• Product Details: images/gallery, description, ingredients/specifications, weight/size, price, discount, stock, vendor
information, reviews and ratings.
• Cart: add/remove products, quantity update, vendor-wise grouping, subtotal, delivery charges, discount, coupon and
taxes.
• Checkout & Payment: delivery address, contact information, vendor-wise summary, delivery charges, discount,
taxes, final payable amount and payment method.
• Order Tracking: order placed, payment confirmed, accepted, processing, packed, shipped, out for delivery,
delivered, cancelled and returned/refunded.
• Reviews: product/vendor ratings, reviews, review images, edit and report inappropriate reviews.
• Complaints: complaint creation, assignment, vendor/admin response, resolution and closure.
4. Multi-Vendor Order Splitting – Core Feature
When a customer buys products from multiple vendors in one checkout, the system should automatically create a
master customer order and separate vendor orders. Each vendor should see and manage only its own
products/orders. Manual forwarding by Admin should not be required.
Example:
Master Customer Order
fi Vendor Order A fi Vendor A
fi Vendor Order B fi Vendor B
fi Vendor Order C fi Vendor C
5. Vendor Panel Requirements
• Vendor registration with mobile/email verification.
• Business information, owner details, business address, bank details, tax information and product categories.
• KYC/document submission: identity proof, address proof, business registration and applicable food-related
licences/certifications.
• Vendor status: Pending Verification, Documents Required, Under Review, Approved, Rejected, Suspended.
• Dashboard: total/new/pending/completed/cancelled orders, total sales, commission, net settlement,
pending/completed payout, product count, low-stock products, reviews and complaints.
• Product management, inventory management and order processing.
• Automated notifications for new orders and vendor orders.
6. Admin Panel Requirements
• Dashboard: total customers, vendors, active vendors, pending verification, products, pending products, orders,
multi-vendor orders, sales, commission, settlements, refunds, complaints, reviews, inventory and revenue.
• Vendor Management: view, approve, reject, suspend vendors; verify documents; manage
profiles/categories/commission; view sales, orders, settlements, complaints and reviews.
• Product approval and quality-control workflow.
• Order management, payment confirmation, cancellation and refunds.
• Commission and vendor settlement/reconciliation.
• Customer complaints and review moderation.
• Reports and basic business analytics.
7. Payment, Commission & Settlement
• Payment gateway integration can use a suitable provider selected by the client.
• Required payment functions: payment success/failure, transaction ID, verification, payment status, history, refund
initiation and reconciliation.
• Marketplace must calculate commission and maintain a vendor ledger.
• Vendor-wise settlement/payout information should be visible to Admin and Vendor.
8. Logistics & WhatsApp
• Shipping integration should support order/vendor-level logistics, tracking and AWB where applicable.
• A suitable logistics provider can be selected based on business requirements.
• WhatsApp API integration should support automated customer/vendor notifications.
• Notifications may include order confirmation, payment confirmation, processing, shipment, delivery, cancellation,
refund and complaint updates.
9. Technology & Infrastructure
• Responsive customer web application; Android/iOS can be considered according to scope.
• Backend/API, database, authentication and role-based access control.
• Cloud infrastructure and scalable architecture.
• Potential technologies previously considered: NestJS, PostgreSQL, Prisma, JWT, AWS S3 or Cloudflare R2. These
should be treated as options unless finalized.
• Security and data protection should be included in the implementation.
10. Critical End-to-End Marketplace Flow
1. Vendor Registration fi KYC/Document Submission fi Admin Verification fi Vendor Approval
2. Vendor fi Product Submission fi Admin Product Approval fi Product Goes Live
3. Customer fi Browse/Search fi Product Details fi Cart fi Checkout fi Online Payment
4. Payment fi Master Order fi Automatic Vendor-wise Order Splitting fi Vendor Processing
5. Packing fi Shipping fi Tracking fi Delivery fi Customer Review
6. Order Completion fi Commission Calculation fi Vendor Ledger fi Settlement/Payout
11. Trust, Quality & Customer Support
• Vendor verification and product approval are important for customer trust.
• Quality/hygiene information should be handled appropriately for food products.
• Customer complaints should cover product quality, damaged/wrong/missing product, delivery, refund, vendor issues
and other issues.
• Admin should have moderation/control over reviews and complaints.
12. What Should Be Confirmed Before Development
• Final commission structure and settlement cycle.
• Final payment gateway and marketplace settlement method.
• Final logistics provider/API and shipping-charge rules.
• Vendor KYC and eligibility criteria.
• Product quality/approval checklist.
• Return, cancellation and refund policy.
• GST/tax treatment and invoice requirements.
• WhatsApp provider/API and message-template requirements.
• Exact MVP scope, timeline, maintenance/support and future-feature pricing.
Reference note: This document consolidates the marketplace requirements and workflows described in the provided Tech Surya IT
Solution quotation for the Vishwaneed multi-vendor rural products marketplace